    <string name="section_watchlist">Your watchlist</string>
    <string name="hint_watchlist">Match by maker ID (first part of the address, like 00:25:DF), by name text, or by a pattern starting with re:. Maker-only router matches are marked possible and never send an alert.</string>
    <string name="section_toggles">What to listen for</string>
    <string name="hint_toggles">Tap a row to switch between Alert (show and buzz), Show only, and Off (ignored completely, not even kept in memory).</string>
    <string name="section_places">Your places</string>
    <string name="hint_places">Save spots you go often. At each one you can stop the buzz for gear you already know is there. Trackers always alert if one follows you, even at home. Gear heard at a place on %1$d+ separate days is labelled “regular”. It’s only a label and never silences anything.</string>
    <string name="section_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="hint_privacy">Saved places, choices and your watchlist are encrypted with a key locked inside this phone. Addresses are kept only as one-way fingerprints, never a record of where you went. No backups, no phone-to-phone transfer, no internet.</string>
